From 29219da3bac9324c9b68adbaa08badb27d8e43a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parth Thakre <144053824+parth-thakre@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:34:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] Split-decode attention: EXL3_DEC_* tuning and the Q4W
 kernel on the dense row layout

Port of 0603ac1 onto dd39a01's dense (query, head) rows. EXL3_DEC_GROUP=1 raises the
row cap from 32 to 128, so a verify step reads each K/V tile once per kv head (q_len 8 with
Qwen3.8's group of 6 is 48 rows: two programs at the cap of 32). With it, the split target is
8 programs per CU for single-token decode and 4 for verify (EXL3_DEC_SPLIT_MULT overrides).
EXL3_DEC_WARPS / STAGES / BLOCK_N override the launch shape in the eager and graph-built paths
alike. EXL3_DEC_Q4W=1 picks the word-sliced split kernel for 4-bit K/V, now with the dense row
indexing. EXL3_DEC_BLOCK_H is gone: the dense layout has no per-program head count. No C++
change, since configure_slot takes the program count from Python now.

gfx1201, synthetic Q4 cache at 60k, one layer: q_len 8 499 us (default 1553), q_len 1 361 us
(default 557), max error 1.9e-6 against the default kernel; the old tree's numbers were 503 and
360.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
